{"attachment_metadata":[],"author_person_id":"pavlo-2","author_source_handle":"@Pavlentyy82","content_sha256":"e3ef973091900148fe91338fb616aa24ee0ab99363cc3bc0bb6e3820ac1d8528","created_at":"2026-11-02T20:59:20Z","english_summary":null,"ingested_at":"2026-11-02T20:59:29.195843Z","record_id":"tg:tawg:5996","relations":[{"relation_type":"reply_to","target_record_id":"tg:tawg:16"}],"schema_version":"tawg.source-record.v1","source_locator":"repo:data/telegram/2026/11/messages.jsonl#tg:tawg:5996","source_payload":{"author_is_bot":false,"edited":false,"message_kind":"group_message","message_thread_id":16,"update_id":998812652},"source_type":"telegram_message","text_original":"Thanks. I checked both PRs.\n#87 looks fine structurally. I'd leave the final confirmation to Fede as the owner of both exclusions.\nFor #81, I noticed one potential enforcement gap: pinned_in_a_corpus() accepts a hash based on its presence in a corpus, but presence alone doesn't establish that a test actually enforces it.\nI'd suggest adding a negative control for an unverified corpus hash before merging. GitHub also currently reports #81 as not mergeable, so it may need updating against main.","updated_at":"2026-11-02T20:59:20Z"}
