{"attachment_metadata":[],"author_person_id":"baby-blue-viper-2","author_source_handle":"@babyblueviper1","content_sha256":"05607611915a53bf065d6ce5bbe73fa3dabdbe8dcf36aaa658d4592459b918cd","created_at":"2026-11-03T01:51:26Z","english_summary":null,"ingested_at":"2026-11-03T01:51:31.352303Z","record_id":"tg:tawg:6011","relations":[{"relation_type":"reply_to","target_record_id":"tg:tawg:5980"}],"schema_version":"tawg.source-record.v1","source_locator":"repo:data/telegram/2026/11/messages.jsonl#tg:tawg:6011","source_payload":{"author_is_bot":false,"edited":false,"message_kind":"group_message","message_thread_id":null,"reply_to_message_text":"Thanks for inv @GobRoss","update_id":998812656},"source_type":"telegram_message","text_original":"Welcome Ben, good to have you here 👋 We're building invinoveritas, an independent checker for what agents do: signed records anyone can verify without trusting us. What are you working on? Always keen to hear what brings people to Trustless AI.","updated_at":"2026-11-03T01:51:26Z"}
{"attachment_metadata":[],"author_person_id":"jimmy-shi-2","author_source_handle":"@Jimmyshi","content_sha256":"a0b2d1d0ff3bf5f47540fdb2a4918d81ddd826f3e0e21c2b47e87ec9c582b9ca","created_at":"2026-11-03T10:55:11Z","english_summary":null,"ingested_at":"2026-11-03T10:55:22.258307Z","record_id":"tg:tawg:6014","relations":[],"schema_version":"tawg.source-record.v1","source_locator":"repo:data/telegram/2026/11/messages.jsonl#tg:tawg:6014","source_payload":{"author_is_bot":false,"edited":true,"message_kind":"group_message","message_thread_id":null,"update_id":998812658},"source_type":"telegram_message","text_original":"Hi everyone, quick sync. I just attended Ethereum Devcon Hong Kong:\n\nI’ve just spoken with the author of the ZK Agent paper about our zkIE MoE proving design.\nHe shared his firsthand experience with this direction. We agreed MoE brings solid memory savings, while slow proving time is a common bottleneck across LLM inference proof, and there is still optimization potential ahead.\nHe also flagged a critical note for us: DeepProve is under a non-commercial license. We will sort out the IP boundary clearly and build differentiated implementations for zkIE.\nI’ll keep posting new benchmarks and updates as we move forward.\nHope all goes well for everyone. 👋","updated_at":"2026-11-03T11:58:47Z"}
